# Code owners for cognium-dev.
#
# Owners are requested automatically on any PR touching a matching path.
# Last match wins, so the specific rules below override the catch-all.
#
# TWO THINGS GATE THIS FILE — until both are done it is inert:
#
#   1. @cogniumhq/coreteam must have WRITE access to this repository.
#      GitHub silently ignores CODEOWNERS entries for a team that lacks
#      write access; no error is surfaced anywhere. At time of writing
#      `GET /repos/cogniumhq/cognium-dev/teams` returns [] — no team has
#      been granted access to this repo at all.
#   2. Branch protection on `main` must enable "Require review from Code
#      Owners". It currently requires nine status checks but no reviews
#      (`required_pull_request_reviews` is null), so owners would be
#      requested but merges would not block.
#
# See #442.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                                   @cogniumhq/coreteam

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supply chain — a change here can execute code on every developer machine
# and every CI run, so these are the paths most worth a second pair of eyes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/.github/                           @cogniumhq/coreteam
/.github/workflows/                 @cogniumhq/coreteam
/release.sh                         @cogniumhq/coreteam
/scripts/                           @cogniumhq/coreteam

# Dependency manifests and the lockfile: the review surface for a malicious
# or typosquatted transitive dependency.
/package.json                       @cogniumhq/coreteam
/package-lock.json                  @cogniumhq/coreteam
/packages/*/package.json            @cogniumhq/coreteam

# Prebuilt binaries cannot be meaningfully diffed in review, so any change
# to one is a deliberate decision rather than an incidental edit.
*.wasm                              @cogniumhq/coreteam

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analysis engine — changes here move detection behaviour, and a regression
# is a missed vulnerability rather than a broken build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/packages/circle-ir/src/analysis/   @cogniumhq/coreteam
/packages/circle-ir/src/core/       @cogniumhq/coreteam

# Security policy.
/SECURITY.md                        @cogniumhq/coreteam
